IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mce-employee`

-- Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions the employee and the employer ask, with the
-- seat and the situation as parameters, for one deployment that serves both.
--
-- ROLES (the seat as a parameter). Every exported question takes `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question
-- about the other role answers `does not arise for you` without reading any other input, so the form never asks its inputs.
--   - `I am an employee` -- the baseline's seat.
--   - `I am an employer` -- new: s 5(1) binds "all employees and employers", and every minimum condition is a duty on the
--     employer (to pay, to give leave, not to refuse it, not to require the hours, to inform and consult).
-- The Western Australian Industrial Relations Commission is not a seat; its State Wage order and casual loading order appear
-- as figures the person supplies.
--
-- SITUATIONS (the graffiti design D8). Within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that situation's fact
-- straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` without reading anything else when the situation does not
-- hold. The questions of one situation share one input, with the same name, type and @desc:
--   - `the employer is a national system employer` (BOOLEAN; both roles): the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 26 excludes this Act
--     for a national system employer and its employees (baseline finding 1), so TRUE gives `does not arise for you` for every
--     minimum condition. The two "does this Act apply" questions take it as an ordinary input and answer no.
--   - `the employment has ended` (BOOLEAN; both roles): s 26 pays out untaken leave "when the employee's employment ends", so
--     FALSE gives `does not arise for you` for the pay-out questions. It comes third, after the national system input.
--
-- The rules are the baseline's (`mce-employee.l4`); this layer calls them and restates none. For the employee the answer is
-- the baseline export's, wrapped in the answer type, wherever the employer is not a national system employer. For the employer
-- the same rules are asked from the other side. No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am an employee`
    `I am an employer`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Hours` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `hours` HAS `how many` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Number of days` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `days` HAS `how many` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- The baseline's MyWork record, built from plain answers; the national system fact is the situation input.
GIVEN `works for hire or reward` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in substance the relationship is employment, not contracting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MyWork
`the work` MEANS MyWork WITH
    `I work for someone for hire or reward` IS `works for hire or reward`
    `in substance the relationship is employment, not contracting` IS `in substance the relationship is employment, not contracting`
    `I am a police officer` IS `a police officer`
    `my employer is a national system employer` IS `the employer is a national system employer`

§§ `For the employee`

§§§ `ss 3, 5, 6A -- does this Act apply to me`

@export Am I an employee for this Act (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 3(1); Industrial Relations Act 1979 (WA) ss 7(1), 7A; s 6A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I work for someone for hire or reward` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are employed by someone to do work for hire or reward (including as an apprentice)
      `in substance the relationship is employment, not contracting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the real substance, practical reality and true nature of the relationship, it is employment and not contracting (IR Act s 7A)
      `I am a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a police officer (s 6A)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I an employee for the purposes of this Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee` THEN `yes if` (`Am I an employee for this Act` (`the work` `I work for someone for hire or reward` `in substance the relationship is employment, not contracting` `I am a police officer` FALSE))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- Arises either way, so the national system fact is an ordinary input here (the same name, type and @desc as the situation).
@export Does this Act give me its minimum conditions (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 5, read with the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 26)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `I work for someone for hire or reward` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are employed by someone to do work for hire or reward (including as an apprentice)
      `in substance the relationship is employment, not contracting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the real substance, practical reality and true nature of the relationship, it is employment and not contracting (IR Act s 7A)
      `I am a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a police officer (s 6A)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does this Act give me its minimum conditions of employment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee` THEN `yes if` (`Does this Act give me its minimum conditions` (`the work` `I work for someone for hire or reward` `in substance the relationship is employment, not contracting` `I am a police officer` `the employer is a national system employer`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does a term of my contract or award that gives me less than a minimum condition bind me (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 5)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the term is less favourable than a minimum condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the term gives the employee less than this Act's minimum
      `the term is a valid agreement to cash out annual leave under s 8` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the term is an agreement to cash out annual leave that meets s 8
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does a term that gives me less than a minimum condition bind me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Does the term bind me` `the term is less favourable than a minimum condition` `the term is a valid agreement to cash out annual leave under s 8`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 8, 9A -- cashing out leave, and maximum hours`

@export Is my agreement to cash out annual leave valid (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 8)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the year of service is complete` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the year of service the leave belongs to has been completed
      `hours forgone under all agreements for that year` IS A NUMBER @desc Total hours of leave given up for that year, this agreement included
      `hours of annual leave earned in that year` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours of paid annual leave the employee became entitled to for that year
      `the employee is paid at least what the leave would have paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment is at least what the employee would have been paid for taking the leave
      `it is in writing signed by employer and employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement is written and signed by both the employer and the employee
      `the job offer was conditional on agreeing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer made signing it a condition of the offer of employment
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my agreement to cash out annual leave valid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is my cash-out agreement valid` `the year of service is complete` `hours forgone under all agreements for that year` `hours of annual leave earned in that year` `the employee is paid at least what the leave would have paid` `it is in writing signed by employer and employee` `the job offer was conditional on agreeing`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What are my ordinary weekly hours for the maximum-hours rule (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 9A(1)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `an award or agreement sets the ordinary hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an industrial instrument covering the employee specifies their ordinary hours
      `the ordinary hours it sets` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly ordinary hours it specifies
GIVETH AN `Hours`
`What are my ordinary weekly hours under the maximum-hours rule` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `hours` (`What are my ordinary weekly hours` `an award or agreement sets the ordinary hours` `the ordinary hours it sets`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I be required or asked to work these hours this week (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) ss 9A, 9B)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `hours this week, counting authorised leave` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours the employee would work this week, with any authorised leave counted as hours worked
      `the ordinary weekly hours` IS A NUMBER @desc The employee's ordinary weekly hours under s 9A(1)(a): those an award or agreement sets, or 38
      `if the extra hours are reasonable under s 9B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For hours beyond ordinary: whether they are reasonable, taking account of safety, family responsibilities, the business, notice and the last 4 weeks' hours
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be required or asked to work these hours this week` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can I be asked to work these hours` `hours this week, counting authorised leave` `the ordinary weekly hours` `if the extra hours are reasonable under s 9B`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 10-14 -- minimum rates of pay`

@export What is my minimum weekly rate of pay (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) ss 12, 13, 14)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the employee's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The employee's age in whole years
      `the employee is an apprentice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is an apprentice
      `the State Wage adult rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly rate for adults who are not apprentices, set by the current State Wage order (IR Act s 50A(1)(a)(i))
      `the State Wage apprentice rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly rate for the employee's class of apprentice, or apprentices generally, set by the State Wage order (IR Act s 50A(1)(a)(ii))
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is my minimum weekly rate of pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`What is my minimum weekly rate` `the employee's age` `the employee is an apprentice` `the State Wage adult rate` `the State Wage apprentice rate`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is my minimum hourly rate of pay (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) ss 10, 11)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the minimum weekly rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The employee's minimum weekly rate under s 12, 13 or 14
      `the employee is casual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is a casual employee (decided on the real substance of the relationship, IR Act s 7B)
      `a higher casual loading set by order, if any` IS A NUMBER @desc A casual loading percentage above 25% set by order under IR Act s 51I; 0 if none
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is my minimum hourly rate of pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`What is my minimum hourly rate` `the minimum weekly rate` `the employee is casual` `a higher casual loading set by order, if any`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 19-21 -- personal leave`

@export How many hours of paid personal leave do I earn each year (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 20)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the employee is casual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is a casual employee (decided on the real substance of the relationship, IR Act s 7B)
      `the hours ordinarily worked each week` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours the employee is ordinarily required to work each week
GIVETH AN `Hours`
`How many hours of paid personal leave do I earn each year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `hours` (`How many hours of personal leave a year` `the employee is casual` `the hours ordinarily worked each week`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I paid for this absence as personal leave (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) ss 19, 20A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `I cannot work because of illness, injury or a family emergency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you cannot work because of your own or a family or household member's illness or injury, or an unexpected emergency affecting a member
      `it is my own illness or injury caused by my serious and wilful misconduct or gross and wilful neglect at work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is your own illness or injury and was caused by your serious and wilful misconduct or gross and wilful neglect in your job
      `I have enough accrued personal leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have enough paid personal leave accrued
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I paid for this absence as personal leave` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Am I paid for this personal leave` `I cannot work because of illness, injury or a family emergency` `it is my own illness or injury caused by my serious and wilful misconduct or gross and wilful neglect at work` `I have enough accrued personal leave`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many days of unpaid personal leave can I take for this occasion (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 21)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `it is a family or household member's illness, injury or emergency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the occasion is a family or household member's illness or injury, or an unexpected emergency affecting one
      `I cannot take paid personal leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you cannot take paid personal leave (for example, a casual, or none accrued)
GIVETH A `Number of days`
`How many days of unpaid personal leave can I take for this occasion` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `days` (`How many days of unpaid personal leave` `it is a family or household member's illness, injury or emergency` `I cannot take paid personal leave`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 23-26 -- paid annual leave`

@export How many hours of paid annual leave do I earn each year (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 23)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the employee is casual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is a casual employee (decided on the real substance of the relationship, IR Act s 7B)
      `the hours ordinarily worked each week` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours the employee is ordinarily required to work each week
GIVETH AN `Hours`
`How many hours of paid annual leave do I earn each year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `hours` (`How many hours of annual leave a year` `the employee is casual` `the hours ordinarily worked each week`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many hours of annual leave have I accrued (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 23(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the employee is casual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is a casual employee (decided on the real substance of the relationship, IR Act s 7B)
      `the hours ordinarily worked each week` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours the employee is ordinarily required to work each week
      `weeks of service, not counting unpaid leave` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of service so far, leaving out unpaid leave
GIVETH AN `Hours`
`How many hours of annual leave have I accrued so far` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `hours` (`How many hours of annual leave accrued` `the employee is casual` `the hours ordinarily worked each week` `weeks of service, not counting unpaid leave`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I insist on taking my annual leave at a time that suits me (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 24)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `employer and employee have agreed when the leave is taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer and the employee have already agreed when the leave will be taken
      `months since the employee became entitled to it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months before the leave starts the employee became entitled to it
      `weeks of notice the employee gives` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks' notice of the leave the employee gives the employer
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I insist on taking my annual leave when it suits me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can I insist on my annual leave` `employer and employee have agreed when the leave is taken` `months since the employee became entitled to it` `weeks of notice the employee gives`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I be paid for my annual leave before it starts (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 25)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the employee asked in writing to be paid in advance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee asked the employer in writing to pay for the leave before it starts
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I be paid for my annual leave before it starts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must I be paid before my leave starts` `the employee asked in writing to be paid in advance`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many hours of untaken annual leave must I be paid out now that my job has ended (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 26)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employment has ended
      `how it ended` IS A HowItEnded @desc How the employment ended
      `untaken hours from completed years` IS A NUMBER @desc Untaken annual leave hours from completed years of service
      `untaken hours from the part-year` IS A NUMBER @desc Untaken annual leave hours from the partly completed year
      `untaken hours from years completed after the misconduct` IS A NUMBER @desc Of the completed-year hours, those from years completed after the misconduct (0 if not dismissed for misconduct)
GIVETH AN `Hours`
`How many hours of untaken annual leave must I be paid out` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE IF NOT `the employment has ended`
             THEN `does not arise for you`
             ELSE `hours` (`How many hours of annual leave must be paid out` `how it ended` `untaken hours from completed years` `untaken hours from the part-year` `untaken hours from years completed after the misconduct`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 27, 30, 31, 39B, 39C -- bereavement leave, public holidays, family and domestic violence leave`

@export How many days of paid bereavement leave do I get (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) ss 3, 27)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `who died` IS A WhoDied @desc Who died, in relation to the employee
GIVETH A `Number of days`
`How many days of paid bereavement leave do I get` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `days` (`How many days of bereavement leave` `who died`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I refuse a request to work on a public holiday (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 30)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `if the request is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the request to work is reasonable, weighing the s 30(4) factors (the business, the work, the employee's circumstances, pay, notice)
      `if the refusal is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a refusal is reasonable, weighing the same factors
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I refuse a request to work on a public holiday` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I refuse to work the public holiday` `if the request is reasonable` `if the refusal is reasonable`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I paid for a public holiday I take off (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 31)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the employee is casual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is a casual employee (decided on the real substance of the relationship, IR Act s 7B)
      `the employee would ordinarily work that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee would ordinarily work on that day
      `the employee is on unpaid leave that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is on unpaid leave that day
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I paid for a public holiday I take off` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Am I paid for the public holiday` `the employee is casual` `the employee would ordinarily work that day` `the employee is on unpaid leave that day`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many days of unpaid family and domestic violence leave can I take now (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) ss 39B, 39C)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `I am experiencing family and domestic violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are experiencing family violence (Restraining Orders Act 1997 s 5A)
      `I need to do something to deal with its impact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you need to do something to deal with its impact
      `I cannot practically do it outside my ordinary hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is impractical to do it outside your ordinary hours of work
      `days already taken in this 12-month period` IS A NUMBER @desc Days of this leave already taken in the current 12-month period of the employment
GIVETH A `Number of days`
`How many days of unpaid family and domestic violence leave can I take now` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `days` (`How many days of family violence leave can I take` `I am experiencing family and domestic violence` `I need to do something to deal with its impact` `I cannot practically do it outside my ordinary hours` `days already taken in this 12-month period`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 40, 41, 43 -- redundancy`

@export Am I entitled to be told of the redundancy and to discuss it with my employer (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 41)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the employee is casual or an apprentice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is a casual employee or an apprentice
      `the employer has decided no one will do the job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer has decided the employee's job will not be done by anyone
      `the employer has decided on a change with a significant effect on the employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer has decided on a major workforce change, loss of job or promotion opportunity, a big change in hours, retraining, transfer or restructure of the job (s 40(2))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I entitled to be told of the redundancy and to discuss it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Am I entitled to be told and consulted` `the employee is casual or an apprentice` `the employer has decided no one will do the job` `the employer has decided on a change with a significant effect on the employee`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many hours of paid leave can I take for job interviews after being told I am redundant (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 43)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the employee is casual or an apprentice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is a casual employee or an apprentice
      `the employee is a seasonal worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is a seasonal worker
      `the employee has been told they are or will be made redundant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer has told the employee that they have been, or will be, made redundant
GIVETH AN `Hours`
`How many hours of paid job interview leave can I take` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employee` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `hours` (`How many hours of job interview leave` `the employee is casual or an apprentice` `the employee is a seasonal worker` `the employee has been told they are or will be made redundant`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the employer`

§§§ `ss 3, 5 -- does this Act bind me`

@export Does this Act bind me in employing this person (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 5(1), read with the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 26)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the person works for me for hire or reward` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you employ the person to do work for hire or reward (including as an apprentice)
      `in substance the relationship is employment, not contracting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the real substance, practical reality and true nature of the relationship, it is employment and not contracting (IR Act s 7A)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does this Act bind me in employing this person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employer` THEN `yes if` (`Does this Act give me its minimum conditions` (`the work` `the person works for me for hire or reward` `in substance the relationship is employment, not contracting` FALSE `the employer is a national system employer`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my agreement with this employee to cash out annual leave valid (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 8)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the year of service is complete` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the year of service the leave belongs to has been completed
      `hours forgone under all agreements for that year` IS A NUMBER @desc Total hours of leave given up for that year, this agreement included
      `hours of annual leave earned in that year` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours of paid annual leave the employee became entitled to for that year
      `the employee is paid at least what the leave would have paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment is at least what the employee would have been paid for taking the leave
      `it is in writing signed by employer and employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement is written and signed by both the employer and the employee
      `the job offer was conditional on agreeing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer made signing it a condition of the offer of employment
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my agreement with this employee to cash out annual leave valid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employer` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is my cash-out agreement valid` `the year of service is complete` `hours forgone under all agreements for that year` `hours of annual leave earned in that year` `the employee is paid at least what the leave would have paid` `it is in writing signed by employer and employee` `the job offer was conditional on agreeing`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 9A, 10-14 -- hours and pay`

@export May I require or ask this employee to work these hours this week (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) ss 9A, 9B)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `hours this week, counting authorised leave` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours the employee would work this week, with any authorised leave counted as hours worked
      `the ordinary weekly hours` IS A NUMBER @desc The employee's ordinary weekly hours under s 9A(1)(a): those an award or agreement sets, or 38
      `if the extra hours are reasonable under s 9B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For hours beyond ordinary: whether they are reasonable, taking account of safety, family responsibilities, the business, notice and the last 4 weeks' hours
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I require this employee to work these hours this week` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employer` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can I be asked to work these hours` `hours this week, counting authorised leave` `the ordinary weekly hours` `if the extra hours are reasonable under s 9B`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the least I must pay this employee each week (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) ss 12, 13, 14)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the employee's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The employee's age in whole years
      `the employee is an apprentice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is an apprentice
      `the State Wage adult rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly rate for adults who are not apprentices, set by the current State Wage order (IR Act s 50A(1)(a)(i))
      `the State Wage apprentice rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly rate for the employee's class of apprentice, or apprentices generally, set by the State Wage order (IR Act s 50A(1)(a)(ii))
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the least I must pay this employee each week` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employer` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`What is my minimum weekly rate` `the employee's age` `the employee is an apprentice` `the State Wage adult rate` `the State Wage apprentice rate`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the least I must pay this employee for each hour worked (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) ss 10, 11)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the minimum weekly rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The employee's minimum weekly rate under s 12, 13 or 14
      `the employee is casual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is a casual employee (decided on the real substance of the relationship, IR Act s 7B)
      `a higher casual loading set by order, if any` IS A NUMBER @desc A casual loading percentage above 25% set by order under IR Act s 51I; 0 if none
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the least I must pay this employee for each hour` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employer` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`What is my minimum hourly rate` `the minimum weekly rate` `the employee is casual` `a higher casual loading set by order, if any`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 20, 23, 24, 26 -- personal and annual leave`

@export How many hours of paid personal leave must I give this employee each year (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 20)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the employee is casual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is a casual employee (decided on the real substance of the relationship, IR Act s 7B)
      `the hours ordinarily worked each week` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours the employee is ordinarily required to work each week
GIVETH AN `Hours`
`How many hours of paid personal leave must I give this employee each year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employer` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `hours` (`How many hours of personal leave a year` `the employee is casual` `the hours ordinarily worked each week`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many hours of paid annual leave must I give this employee each year (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 23)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the employee is casual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is a casual employee (decided on the real substance of the relationship, IR Act s 7B)
      `the hours ordinarily worked each week` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours the employee is ordinarily required to work each week
GIVETH AN `Hours`
`How many hours of paid annual leave must I give this employee each year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employer` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `hours` (`How many hours of annual leave a year` `the employee is casual` `the hours ordinarily worked each week`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 24(1): "the employer must not refuse the employee taking, at a time suitable to the employee," leave the employee became
-- entitled to more than 12 months before. So the employer may refuse exactly when the employee cannot insist.
@export May I refuse to let this employee take annual leave at the time they want (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 24)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `employer and employee have agreed when the leave is taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer and the employee have already agreed when the leave will be taken
      `months since the employee became entitled to it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months before the leave starts the employee became entitled to it
      `weeks of notice the employee gives` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks' notice of the leave the employee gives the employer
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I refuse to let this employee take annual leave when they want` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employer` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (NOT (`Can I insist on my annual leave` `employer and employee have agreed when the leave is taken` `months since the employee became entitled to it` `weeks of notice the employee gives`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many hours of untaken annual leave must I pay out to this employee now that the employment has ended (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 26)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the employment has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employment has ended
      `how it ended` IS A HowItEnded @desc How the employment ended
      `untaken hours from completed years` IS A NUMBER @desc Untaken annual leave hours from completed years of service
      `untaken hours from the part-year` IS A NUMBER @desc Untaken annual leave hours from the partly completed year
      `untaken hours from years completed after the misconduct` IS A NUMBER @desc Of the completed-year hours, those from years completed after the misconduct (0 if not dismissed for misconduct)
GIVETH AN `Hours`
`How many hours of untaken annual leave must I pay out to this employee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employer` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE IF NOT `the employment has ended`
             THEN `does not arise for you`
             ELSE `hours` (`How many hours of annual leave must be paid out` `how it ended` `untaken hours from completed years` `untaken hours from the part-year` `untaken hours from years completed after the misconduct`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 27, 30, 31, 39B, 39C -- bereavement leave, public holidays, family and domestic violence leave`

@export How many days of paid bereavement leave must I give this employee (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) ss 3, 27)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `who died` IS A WhoDied @desc Who died, in relation to the employee
GIVETH A `Number of days`
`How many days of paid bereavement leave must I give this employee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employer` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `days` (`How many days of bereavement leave` `who died`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May this employee refuse my request to work on a public holiday (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 30)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `if the request is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the request to work is reasonable, weighing the s 30(4) factors (the business, the work, the employee's circumstances, pay, notice)
      `if the refusal is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a refusal is reasonable, weighing the same factors
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May this employee refuse my request to work on a public holiday` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employer` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I refuse to work the public holiday` `if the request is reasonable` `if the refusal is reasonable`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I pay this employee for a public holiday they take off (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 31)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the employee is casual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is a casual employee (decided on the real substance of the relationship, IR Act s 7B)
      `the employee would ordinarily work that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee would ordinarily work on that day
      `the employee is on unpaid leave that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is on unpaid leave that day
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I pay this employee for a public holiday they take off` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employer` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Am I paid for the public holiday` `the employee is casual` `the employee would ordinarily work that day` `the employee is on unpaid leave that day`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 39C: the conditions are the employee's; the employer may ask for evidence (s 39D, not encoded). Asked from the employer's
-- side with the employee's facts.
@export How many days of unpaid family and domestic violence leave must I allow this employee now (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) ss 39B, 39C)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the employee is experiencing family and domestic violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is experiencing family violence (Restraining Orders Act 1997 s 5A)
      `the employee needs to do something to deal with its impact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee needs to do something to deal with its impact
      `the employee cannot practically do it outside ordinary hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is impractical for the employee to do it outside their ordinary hours of work
      `days already taken in this 12-month period` IS A NUMBER @desc Days of this leave already taken in the current 12-month period of the employment
GIVETH A `Number of days`
`How many days of unpaid family and domestic violence leave must I allow` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employer` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `days` (`How many days of family violence leave can I take` `the employee is experiencing family and domestic violence` `the employee needs to do something to deal with its impact` `the employee cannot practically do it outside ordinary hours` `days already taken in this 12-month period`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 40, 41, 43 -- redundancy`

@export Must I tell this employee of the redundancy, or the change, and discuss it with them (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 41)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the employee is casual or an apprentice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is a casual employee or an apprentice
      `the employer has decided no one will do the job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer has decided the employee's job will not be done by anyone
      `the employer has decided on a change with a significant effect on the employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer has decided on a major workforce change, loss of job or promotion opportunity, a big change in hours, retraining, transfer or restructure of the job (s 40(2))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I tell this employee of the redundancy and discuss it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employer` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Am I entitled to be told and consulted` `the employee is casual or an apprentice` `the employer has decided no one will do the job` `the employer has decided on a change with a significant effect on the employee`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many hours of paid leave for job interviews must I give this employee after telling them they are redundant (Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993 (WA) s 43)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the employer is a national system employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a national system employer under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s 14 (for example, a company trading in Western Australia); if so, this Act gives nothing (Fair Work Act s 26)
      `the employee is casual or an apprentice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is a casual employee or an apprentice
      `the employee is a seasonal worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is a seasonal worker
      `the employee has been told they are or will be made redundant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer has told the employee that they have been, or will be, made redundant
GIVETH AN `Hours`
`How many hours of paid job interview leave must I give this employee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am an employer` THEN
        IF `the employer is a national system employer`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `hours` (`How many hours of job interview leave` `the employee is casual or an apprentice` `the employee is a seasonal worker` `the employee has been told they are or will be made redundant`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
